  },
  "bio": [
   {
    "text": "In 2014 it is described as a rolling region of Zendikar that Nahiri senses through the earth.",
    "cites": [
     "p:stories/the-lithomancer"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/the-lithomancer"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "In 2015 Nahiri crushes Eldrazi with an avalanche and then enters a ruined kor city in Ondu, where she remembers her old life.",
    "cites": [
     "stirring-slumber-2015-05-13-e5",
     "p:stories/stirring-slumber-2015-05-13"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/stirring-slumber-2015-05-13#:~:text=sent%20an%20avalanche%20to%20crush%20the%20abominations",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/stirring-slumber-2015-05-13"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "There she finds a carving of herself with a Kozilek-like figure, named 'Nahiri the Prophet, Voice of Talib', and collapses the building, blaming herself for calling Kozilek a god.",
    "cites": [
     "stirring-slumber-2015-05-13-e6"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/stirring-slumber-2015-05-13#:~:text=%22Nahiri%20the%20Prophet%2C%20Voice%20of%20Talib.%22"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Another page mentions a coast near the Yawning Chasm.",
    "cites": [
     "p:stories/beneath-surface-2016-01-27"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/beneath-surface-2016-01-27"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "In 2020 it is named as the place where Zareth got his Skyclave hooks and as the continent where Orien was lost.",
    "cites": [
     "p:stories/red-route-2020-09-04",
     "p:stories/hunger-2020-09-25"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/red-route-2020-09-04",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/hunger-2020-09-25"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "status": {
   "text": "As of its last mention in September 2020 it is a Zendikari continent, named as where Orien was lost.",
